According to http://h30097.www3.hp.com/cplus/spd.html, libcxxma.so is
not considered a file in the "RTL image". So, we cannot legally
redistribute libcxxma.so if we were to create our own CXXREDIST651V37
bundle for customers. Was this simply a typo? If libcxx.so is
redistributable, then it makes sense to allow libcxxma.so to be
redistributed as well. Neither the CXXLIB651 nor CXXLIB710 packages
contain libcxxma.so.

