Connectivity is working.  However, there is a restriction in Tru64 Unix 5.1.
It cannot use a filter on a rm/rp printer.  I called HP support yesterday
and they sent me a document describing how to work around this restriction.
Basically, it takes two printcap entries.  The first one is the one that
people print to and it applies the filters and then forwards the resulting
print job to the second printer which then uses rm/rp to send it to the
Windows Server.  This isn't in the on-line HP documentation for Tru64 Unix.

The reponse to "lpq -PWAKE" below shows that port 515 is passing data.  If
it weren't, lpq wouldn't show the status of the Windows 2000 print queue.

Mike.

